Thread the mouse EVENT-HANDLER's button-sub-handler dispatch args (FUN_1000_39d7 -> d5ac = MGAVIDEO 2f03).

FUN_1000_39d7 is the engine's INT-33h mouse event handler (installed via fn 0x14, mask 0x1f).  On a button
event (AX & 0x7e) it far-calls the driver's click sub-handler DGROUP:0x5ac (= MGAVIDEO FUN_0000_2f03).  The
asm (0x139d7..0x13a28) reaches `call DWORD ds:0x15ac` with AX = the DOS condition mask (event flags) and BX
= dd9c (the masked button state, just stored two instructions earlier).  FUN_0000_2f03 reads exactly those:
param_1 = AX (tested `& 6 / & 0x18 / & 0x60` for the left/right/middle button-event groups) and param_2 = BX
(stored to d5b6, the live button state, then dispatched to the event-enqueue callback c3fe).  Ghidra's
__allregs indirect-vector site dropped both operands (`(*d5ac)()`), so 2f03 saw garbage flags/buttons and
mis-dispatched (or spuriously fired) the click.  Thread them faithfully: (param_1 = event flags, dd9c =
button state).  Per-patch indirect-vector arg threading, CLAUDE.md doctrine.  Asm-verified at 0x13a22.
--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -45076,7 +45076,7 @@
   if ((param_1 & 0x7e) == 0) {
     return;
   }
-  (*(code *)fist_icall_far((uint32_t)(DAT_1000_d5ac)))();
+  (*(code *)fist_icall_far((uint32_t)(DAT_1000_d5ac)))(param_1,DAT_1000_dd9c);
   return;
 }
 
